From: semimikoh <ejffjeosms@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 10:33:40 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Add design note: underline composing IME text

Design note for issue #342. Composing (uncommitted) IME text is drawn
with no underline, so there is no cue that it is mid-composition; native
text fields and Google Docs underline it. The composing text already
lives on a view-local render path (injectComposingInline splices it into
the block layout without touching the model, see #318/#332 and #346), so
the underline is a paint-time decoration of that injected run and never
reaches the document model.

The note proposes a view-local `composing` marker set by
composingStyleFrom and a thin solid underline drawn in renderRun,
covering both the browser IME and software-Hangul assembler paths.
Design-note-first; implementation to follow on this branch.
